inline_comments.body:
Triton includes pointer alignment in the specialization key. MRV1 DBO passes seq_lens[request_slice] / block_table_tensor[request_slice] views straight into this kernel (ubatch_utils.py:278/316). The DBO assert at gpu_model_runner.py:2502 only fires with spec decode, and without spec decode hybrid + --enable-dbo falls back to MRV1. When the second ubatch starts at a request index that isn't a multiple of 4, a new variant JIT-compiles mid-step. I measured 25–28 ms cold and ~1.5 ms with a warm cache, and it raises under jit_monitor_mode=error. The torch path it replaces never JIT-compiled. Adding the argument below removes the extra variant with no measurable device or host cost:
suggestion
@triton.jit(do_not_specialize_on_alignment=["out_ptr", "block_table_ptr", "seq_lens_ptr"])
